# Application version

The application version is the `version` field in `backend/Cargo.toml`. Startup logs it via `env!("CARGO_PKG_VERSION")`. Dependency versions in that file are not the application version.

When a change ships user-visible or behavioral work, bump that version in the same change using [semantic versioning](https://semver.org/) (`MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH`):

- **PATCH** — bug fix or internal change with no new behavior (`1.1.1` → `1.1.2`)
- **MINOR** — backward-compatible feature or capability (`1.1.1` → `1.2.0`)
- **MAJOR** — breaking change to stored data, config, or external behavior (`1.1.1` → `2.0.0`)

Read the current version from `Cargo.toml` before editing it. Reset lower segments to `0` when a higher segment increases. Do not bump the version for docs-only, comment-only, or design-only changes.
